- The OpenAPI `Owner`/`OwnerFields` schemas define NO `householdId` property (so the generated `OwnerDto` will not serialize one).
- `OwnerMapper` / `RespondWithOwnerCreated` never set or emit a `householdId`.
- The POST pipeline's `RejectDuplicateOwnerHousehold` only lets `sharesHousehold` requests pass through; nothing computes or persists a shared household identifier.

So the create/POST flow currently has no `householdId` support, and this test would fail against the present code.

