`OwnerFields` schema (request DTO — `OwnerFieldsDto`), openapi.yml lines 1991-2056:
```yaml
    OwnerFields:
      title: Owner fields
      description: Editable fields of a pet owner.
      type: object
      properties:
        firstName:   # string, 1..30, pattern letters, example George
        lastName:    # string, 1..30, pattern letters, example Franklin
        address:     # string, 1..255, example '110 W. Liberty St.'
        city:        # string, 1..80, example Madison
        telephone:   # string, 1..20, pattern '^[0-9]*$', example '6085551023'
        email:       # string, max 255, "stored and returned lower-cased"
        registrationDate:  # string, format date, defaults to server current date
        sharesHousehold:   # boolean; when true allow same last name+address
      required:
        - firstName
        - lastName
        - address
        - city
        - telephone
```

`Owner` schema (response DTO — `OwnerDto`), openapi.yml lines 2057-2098 — allOf OwnerFields plus:
```yaml
    Owner:
      allOf:
        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OwnerFields'
        - type: object
          properties:
            id:            # integer int32, readOnly
            displayName:   # 'LastName, FirstName', readOnly
            initials:      # 'G.F.', readOnly
            customerCode:  # '<LAST3>-<NNNN>' e.g. 'SMI-0007', readOnly
            pets:          # array of Pet, readOnly
          required:
            - pets
```

Neither DTO schema declares a `householdId` field. The only household-related property is the boolean request input `sharesHousehold`.

## 5. OwnerRepository: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`

```java
