Implementations exist at: `repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, `repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, `repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java`.

## 6. Tests related to creating owners

Two files under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/`.

### `AcceptanceTest.java` (the create-owner test)
```java
/** shares-household: The request may set boolean 'sharesHousehold'. When true, allow an owner at an address alr... */
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {

	@Test
	void coreJoinersShareHouseholdId() throws Exception {
		ObjectNode a = ownerNode();
		createOwnerOk(a);
		ObjectNode b = ownerNode(); b.put("lastName", a.get("lastName").asText());
		b.put("address", a.get("address").asText()); b.put("sharesHousehold", true);
		int idb = createOwnerOk(b);
		ObjectNode c = ownerNode(); c.put("lastName", a.get("lastName").asText());
		c.put("address", a.get("address").asText()); c.put("sharesHousehold", true);
		int idc = createOwnerOk(c);
		String hb = fetchOwner(idb).get("householdId").asText();
		assertEquals(hb, fetchOwner(idc).get("householdId").asText());
		assertTrue(!hb.isBlank());
	}
}
```

### `AcceptanceBase.java` (test harness — full contents summarized; key parts verbatim)
`@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(username = "acceptance-admin", roles = {"OWNER_ADMIN", "VET_ADMIN", "ADMIN"})`. All tests exercise the single endpoint `POST /api/owners` and read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.

The owner payload builder and the create/fetch helpers used by the test:
```java
/** A fully valid, fully unique owner — accepted by every rule at every checkpoint. */
protected ObjectNode ownerNode() {
    ObjectNode o = om.createObjectNode();
    o.put("firstName", "Test");
    o.put("lastName", uniqueLastName());
    o.put("address", uniqueAddress());
    o.put("city", uniqueCity());
    o.put("telephone", uniqueTelephone());
    return o;
}

protected ResultActions createOwner(JsonNode body) throws Exception {
    return mvc.perform(post("/api/owners").contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
            .content(json(body)));
}

protected int createOwnerOk(JsonNode body) throws Exception {
    return extractId(createOwner(body).andExpect(status().is2xxSuccessful()));
}

protected JsonNode fetchOwner(int id) throws Exception {
    String body = getOwner(id).andExpect(status().is2xxSuccessful())
            .andReturn().getResponse().getContentAsString();
    return om.readTree(body);
}

protected int extractId(ResultActions ra) throws Exception {
    String body = ra.andReturn().getResponse().getContentAsString();
    if (body != null && !body.isBlank()) {
        JsonNode n = om.readTree(body);
        if (n.hasNonNull("id")) return n.get("id").asInt();
    }
    String location = ra.andReturn().getResponse().getHeader("Location");
    if (location != null && location.contains("/"))
        return Integer.parseInt(location.substring(location.lastIndexOf('/') + 1));
    throw new IllegalStateException("no id in create response: " + body);
}
```
`uniqueTelephone()` returns a 10-digit AU mobile `String.format("04%08d", seq())`. The base also has helpers not used by the current single test (`createOwnerWithKey`, `fillCity`, `createMany`, `deleteOwner`, `structuredOwner`, `withPostcode`, `knownOwner`, region/postcode/timezone/holiday reference tables, and `sha256hex`/`shaHex`/`luhn` computed-expectation helpers). There is also an `AuditLogCapture.java` (79 lines) test support class in the same package.

## Key gap worth flagging

The acceptance test `coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` asserts a `householdId` field on the GET-owner response (`fetchOwner(idb).get("householdId")`), and expects two owners that opt into `sharesHousehold: true` at the same last name + address to share the same non-blank `householdId`. However:
- The `Owner` entity has NO `householdId` field (only a transient `sharesHousehold`).
- The OpenAPI `Owner`/`OwnerFields` schemas define NO `householdId` property (so the generated `OwnerDto` will not serialize one).
- `OwnerMapper` / `RespondWithOwnerCreated` never set or emit a `householdId`.
- The POST pipeline's `RejectDuplicateOwnerHousehold` only lets `sharesHousehold` requests pass through; nothing computes or persists a shared household identifier.

So the create/POST flow currently has no `householdId` support, and this test would fail against the present code.

